atlas commands-recursive-owner

architecture recursive-substrate-native-owner
  canonical_name RecursiveSubstrateNativeOwner
  family commands
  domain Execution / Recursive substrate and representation integrity
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Can recursive context, native token bodies, deltas and mission evidence share one durable owner without granting representations semantic authority?
  purpose Retire the Python recursive service and CLI into Bun orchestration over existing SQLite state and the real native Rust token engine.
  node_types CanonicalArtifact
  node_types TokenBody
  node_types DependencyEdge
  node_types LogicalDelta
  node_types RuntimeImage
  node_types HashLinkedReceipt
  internal_calculus canonical bytes -> native token chunks -> shared body identity with explicit semantic ownership edges -> verified delta reconstruction -> affected dependency closure
  internal_calculus mission attempt receipt -> sequential local candidate writes -> completion or uncertain receipt -> explicit reconciliation before retry
  invariant identical token bytes may share physical identity without merging distinct artifact owners
  invariant source paths are explicit authenticated inputs; generated files stay confined to the owner root
  invariant historical receipts preserve raw numeric and Unicode digest semantics; corrupt cached bodies cannot become reusable evidence
  invariant read-only catalog hints cannot allow known closure writes to bypass serialized effect scheduling
  invariant runtime images require valid receipt and flux chains; BFP plans remain candidates and never activate authority
  forbidden_inference exact fallback tokenizer or successful COPY reconstruction -> compatibility with a vendor model tokenizer or model KV cache
  forbidden_inference complete local tool witness -> distributed transaction atomicity, production write authorization or estate-wide performance
