  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_store.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_schema.sql
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_catalog.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMcp/src/clis.c
  source_path integrations/mcp/canonical_json.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/mission_plan.mjs
  invariant task-bearing mission bundles recompute and bind one semantic task-plan digest across all seven IRs; execution plans remain candidate-only
  known_gap task-plan binding is implemented and tested in source but is not part of the earlier live cutover witness
  source_path deploy/launchd/service_cutover.mjs
  source_path deploy/launchd/recursive_cutover.mjs
  source_path deploy/launchd/bonfyre-recursive
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_store.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_transport.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreMcp/tests/vectors.sh check replays 44 recursive command vectors recorded from the retired recursive_cli.mjs (grammar, catalog validation, mission files, native-smoke, wire refusals) against bonfyre-mcp byte for byte
  witness deploy/launchd/tests/service_cutover.test.mjs verifies the complete legacy table signature and additive indexes for rollback compatibility
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_integration.test.mjs
  witness tests/recursive_native_witness.mjs exercises all twenty-two tools with real native token compilation and exact reconstruction in disposable state
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_python_baseline.json read-only live Python baseline, not a native deployment claim
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_legacy_snapshot.json verifies all 134 historical receipts and four flux streams on a disposable database copy
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_cutover.json records live daemon and CLI retirement, unchanged chains and counts, refreshed consumers and a measured replay-latency regression
  known_gap initial 25-sample live replay benchmark regressed from 57.5 to 68.6 milliseconds median; no throughput or scaling win is established
  known_gap native integration requires an installed real token engine; unavailable engines are explicitly skipped rather than simulated in CI
  known_gap compound operations can leave partial candidate state; durable attempt receipts require reconciliation and do not claim automatic rollback
  known_gap native token engine is an installed independent owner; source-level retirement does not claim ownership of that implementation

